    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "60bdf5ea_d1b49364",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-13T13:51:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I noticed that `RestrictedForEnvironment` is repeatable and can also have multiple `environments`. Given the former, the latter seems unnecessary.\n\nDo you have a specific use case in mind where you would supply more than one environment per annotation instance?",
      "revId": "a754f8afdba6ad784ad2601164663e4cde86c42c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bea14642_fcc867f1",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1439319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-14T14:27:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s just for ease of use between environments that share common restrictions. We don\u0027t have specific use case at the moment, but we kept it open for future.\n\nIsolated Process has lots of common restriction with SdkSandbox, but nobody is working on adding those annotation currently. We might have more sandbox in future (discussion ongoing) with similar restriction.\n\nRepetable is for situations where restrictions diverge. I think most of the time, it will be the same (hence list for env) and \"repetable\" helps with exceptions.",
      "parentUuid": "60bdf5ea_d1b49364",
      "revId": "a754f8afdba6ad784ad2601164663e4cde86c42c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4fb07b41_bd22dca6",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-14T14:31:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, you think it likely that multiple environments will add a restriction at the same level? I suppose it makes sense that an API that needs restricting in one environment is likely to need restricting in another environment. It also makes sense to try and add those restrictions at the same API version.\n\nThanks.\n\n@nanaasiedu@google.com - fyi",
      "parentUuid": "bea14642_fcc867f1",
      "revId": "a754f8afdba6ad784ad2601164663e4cde86c42c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ca736e05_6f0dd33e",
        "filename": "core/java/android/hardware/usb/UsbManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T16:42:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks as though `SDK_SANDBOX` has a string representation of \"SDK Runtime\". Although that is in the body of the `toString()` method. Metalava cannot access them. So, we would either need to hard code that `SDK_SANDBOX -\u003e SDK Runtime` or there will need to be some other way to specify the string representation.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "a754f8afdba6ad784ad2601164663e4cde86c42c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9fe7ec22_a78d01a4",
        "filename": "core/java/android/hardware/usb/UsbManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1439319
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T17:14:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Metalava cannot access them. So, we would either need to hard code that SDK_SANDBOX -\u003e SDK Runtime\n\nI am fine with hard coding it, but why can\u0027t Metalava access the public enum? I was able to access it using reflection in the test: https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:frameworks/libs/modules-utils/javatests/android/annotation/RestrictedForEnvironmentTests.java;l\u003d67?q\u003dRestrictedForEnvironment\u0026sq\u003drepo:googleplex-android%2Fplatform%2Fsuperproject%2Fmain%20b:main",
      "parentUuid": "ca736e05_6f0dd33e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "a754f8afdba6ad784ad2601164663e4cde86c42c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c66732d9_15adbdb1",
        "filename": "core/java/android/hardware/usb/UsbManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 79,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-17T15:58:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Metalava can access the enum what it cannot do is determine its string representation. That involves looking in the body of the `toString()` method and that is just too complicated and too much effort for too little benefit. Part of the complication is that it requires digging into implementation specific details of the different backends and will not work at all in those that do not provide access to method bodies. It is also very fragile as even a minor change to the body could break the logic.",
      "parentUuid": "9fe7ec22_a78d01a4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 41,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 52
      },
      "revId": "a754f8afdba6ad784ad2601164663e4cde86c42c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
